  "tale": "Earth lives inside his alternation and would die outside it. Crops need the dark as surely as the light; bodies need sleep as surely as waking; the sea needs the tide to go out as surely as to come in. His heroism is the rhythm itself — the year turning, the heart resting between beats, work answered by rest and rest by work. Every farmer who lets a field lie fallow, every law that limits power with its opposite, every person who can hold two true things at once without breaking — that is Kyreason's mastery, quietly keeping the world from tipping into either of its extremes.",
