  "tale": "Earth's debt to him is rest and humility. Night is his gift repeated daily: the dark in which bodies repair, wounds close, and minds dream the dreams Sound turns into imagination. The deep ocean, the unmapped cave, the space between stars — his territories are why Earth still has frontiers, and why no generation gets to mistake its knowledge for the whole of things. His heroism is unglamorous and total: he keeps the world bigger than anyone's account of it, so that wonder, caution, and searching never run out. Every explorer, every scientist at a dark microscope, every child asking a question no one can answer yet walks in his keeping. ## Batch — Soul & Spirit / Death & Ending",
