  "origin": "When ysgnutcoh's will split into two spirits, Kyreason's second line was Matter — the dream given weight. Before him, the world the Emperor had lived in his dream was idea and light; Matter made it substance, something that could be stood on, held, and built with. From him came Value, Tools, and Minerals, and for a time the Elements were his too — until Hoc moved the God of Elements into Life's house, because the elements behave like living things. Matter did not protest the parting. What remains his is the ground of everything: all that has mass answers to him.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Matter fully masters God of Matter in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of matter, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Physical Matter & Energy\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "Earth's debt to him is everything solid it stands on. Every foundation poured, every wall raised, every tool lifted is his domain keeping its promise that things hold. When engineers test concrete before a dam is filled, when a mason taps a brick and listens, they are checking his workmanship. His heroism is the unnoticed kind: the floor that does not give way, the hull that does not split, the roof that stays over a sleeping family in a storm. A world made of unreliable substance could hold no one. He makes sure it holds everyone.",
  "job": "To measure and combine matter where needed; to separate its proper operation; and to support the world's wellbeing through responsible mastery of this domain.",
