   "power": "His mastery is substance itself — everything that takes up room and can be weighed. He understands matter completely: what it is made of, how it holds together, how it breaks, how it can be shaped without being ruined. Nothing material happens outside his knowing, from the stone in a field to the steel in a bridge. His power is quiet because it is foundational: he does not perform wonders with substance; he is the reason substance is reliable enough for wonders to be built on it.",
   "origin": "When ysgnutcoh's will split into two spirits, Kyreason's second line was Matter — the dream given weight. Before him, the world the Emperor had lived in his dream was idea and light; Matter made it substance, something that could be stood on, held, and built with. From him came Value, Tools, and Minerals, and for a time the Elements were his too — until Hoc moved the God of Elements into Life's house, because the elements behave like living things. Matter did not protest the parting. What remains his is the ground of everything: all that has mass answers to him."
