  "house": "Kyreason's line",
  "wisdom": "Check your mixture: are you all fire and no water, all earth and no air? A life out of balance does not need a new life — it needs one element added and one taken away.",
  "origin": "The God of Elements was born in Matter's house, the child who took substance and gave it behavior: burning, flowing, breathing, standing firm. Then Hoc moved him — out of Matter's house and into the house of Life, placed between Culture and Spirit, and all his children moved with him: Fire, Water, Air, and Earth. One did not move with him: the God of Sound, once under Air, whom Hoc raised out of the whole subtree to stand as First God. The move itself is the Elements' doctrine — he was re-homed because the elements do not behave like dead stuff. They behave like living things.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Elements fully masters God of Elements in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of elements, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Physical Matter & Energy\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "Earth runs on his household's cooperation. Rain falls (water and air), gathers in soil (earth), and the sun's fire drives the whole turning — the water cycle every schoolchild learns is his family at work. Farmers live by his children's treaties: enough rain but not flood, sun but not drought, soil that holds the seed. When a wildfire is stopped by a river and a wind shift, that is his household negotiating. His heroism is balance at planetary scale: the elements, held in one keeping, serve life instead of taking turns destroying it.",
