  "origin": "Minerals is a direct child of Matter, standing beside Value and Tools in his father's house — though his record holds a wandering: he was placed for a time under the God of Biology, among the body's workings, before Hoc moved him back under Matter where he belongs. The wandering suits him; he is the one god both houses could claim, since the body is built from him as surely as the mountain is. He is the earth's stored riches in their raw state: the Heart's treasury, still unopened, worth still in the ground.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Minerals fully masters God of Minerals in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of minerals, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Physical Matter & Energy\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "Earth's heroism in his name begins with salt — the mineral so vital that roads, wages, and wars were once built around it, and a body without it dies. Then iron for the plow, phosphate for the field that feeds a city, lithium for the battery in a rescue radio. And the miners themselves stand inside his heroism: the crews who go down into his dark before dawn so that the surface world can have light, heat, and tools — ordinary people doing the most dangerous ordinary work on Earth, in his house, on his terms. He is the god of what the earth saved up so life could spend it.",
  "job": "To measure and combine minerals where needed; to separate its proper operation; and to support the world's wellbeing through responsible mastery of this domain.",
  "number": 17,
  "founderArchive": {
   "role": "the earth's stored riches in their raw state; direct child of Matter, beside Value and Tools.",
   "job": "The earth's stored riches in their raw state",
   "function": "he is the Heart's treasury unopened — worth still in the ground.",
   "power": "His mastery is the mineral wealth of the earth, completely understood: every ore, salt, stone, and crystal, where it lies and what it is good for. Nothing buried is hidden from him. His domain joins the two scales of Earth at once — the zinc and iron in a child's blood and the zinc and iron in the hillside are one substance in his keeping. His power is stored time: minerals are the planet's long patience, laid down over ages, and he is the keeper of the vault. To mine is to make a withdrawal from an account he alone can audit in full.",
   "origin": "Minerals is a direct child of Matter, standing beside Value and Tools in his father's house — though his record holds a wandering: he was placed for a time under the God of Biology, among the body's workings, before Hoc moved him back under Matter where he belongs. The wandering suits him; he is the one god both houses could claim, since the body is built from him as surely as the mountain is. He is the earth's stored riches in their raw state: the Heart's treasury, still unopened, worth still in the ground."
  },
