  "name": "God of Nature",
  "role": "Divine steward of Nature: the living world as a whole; child of World, father of Sky, Ocean, and Land.. This God holds a distinct responsibility within organisms in their environments, habitats, ecological relationships, and natural cycles.",
  "function": "Within the world, this God helps organisms in their environments, habitats, ecological relationships, and natural cycles. Their contribution is to make nature understandable, dependable, and beneficial, while cooperating with other domains rather than replacing them.",
