  "wisdom": "Plant before you cut. Before you spend the savings, take the time, or use the friend — put the seed back in the ground first, so that what you take is already growing again.",
  "origin": "Wood is Earth's second child — the ground's substance persuaded to live. Where his brother Metal is earth taken down into the dark, Wood is earth risen up: root in his father's keeping, crown in the sky's, the tree standing as a treaty between the two. He was born when substance first grew — when matter stopped merely lasting and started reaching. Everything wooden carries his double nature: it is the only building material that was once alive, and it keeps the memory of growth in its grain. He is the Heart's patience in matter: strength that took its time.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Wood fully masters God of Wood in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of wood, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Physical Matter & Energy\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "Earth's heroism in his name holds roofs over more people than any other substance. The timber frame of a farmhouse, the scaffold, the cradle, the boat that first crossed a river — his domain is civilization's first technology and still its warmest. When a village rebuilds after a storm, it rebuilds in wood first, because wood forgives: it can be cut by hand, nailed by neighbors, repaired by grandchildren. And in the forests still standing, his living form does quieter work — holding hillsides against the rain, shading the streams where fish spawn. He is the god who grows his own temples and then lets people live in them.",
