   "function": "he is the Heart's patience in matter — growth you can build with.",
   "power": "His mastery is wood and the woody growth of the world: timber, grain, and the living architecture of trees. He understands completely how a tree builds itself — ring by ring, season by season — and how that building can serve after the tree's life: beam, board, hull, handle. Nothing grown of wood is outside his knowing. His power is time made usable: a plank is decades of summers, stored in a form a carpenter can cut in an afternoon. He teaches what his brother cannot — that some strength only exists because it grew slowly and was allowed to flex.",
