  "house": "Kyreason's line",
  "origin": "Soul was not born in Life's house but in Worth's — a child of God of Worth, under Value, under Matter — and the placement is the doctrine: a soul is a thing of *weight*. Life gives the flame; Worth gives the measure. Soul is the light in a person that can be weighed, read, and cleansed — cleansed of darkness and restored to its original innocence, which is the heart of this religion. From him descend Readings, Cleanse, and Passion, double-seated: the soul examined, the soul restored, and everything a life has learned gathered into a single conscious.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Soul fully masters God of Soul in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of soul, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Soul & Spirituality\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "Every act of conscience on Earth is his domain at work. The shopkeeper who corrects a till error no one saw; the man who, years later, finds the person he wronged and says so plainly — they are weighing something, and the scale is his. Prisons, confessionals, twelve-step rooms, and quiet apologies across kitchen tables all run on his premise: that a person can be read honestly, found darkened, and still be restorable. Earth does not run on perfect people. It runs on people who believe a soul can come clear again.",
  "job": "To discern and guide soul where needed; to reconcile its proper operation; and to support the world's wellbeing through responsible mastery of this domain.",
