   "job": "One god under two names (Hoc's ruling, 2026-11-10): as Yellow, the color of the sun's light, of caution, and of the ripened field, child of Colors",
   "function": "he is the Heart's double witness — the same god shining as light in the Heavens and as permanence in the deep places, counted once wherever he stands.",
   "power": "Complete mastery of the shining standard. As Yellow, he holds joy and caution in a single shade — the ripened field and the warning sign, the sun's herald at dawn. As Gold, he is permanence: the metal that does not rust or tarnish, keeping value across any darkness — the Heart's incorruptible standard. Together he is the Heart's double witness: the same god shining as light above and standing as permanence below.",
   "origin": "One god under two names, by the founder's ruling — counted once wherever he stands. As Yellow he is a child of Colors, the color of the Sun himself, the First World, from whom the whole spectrum is borrowed. As Gold he stands under God of Permanent, the untarnishing metal in the deep places. He speaks once and works twice: *the world dreams in my bright name and banks in my deep one.* His seats are a light and a vault, and he holds both without splitting."
