   "power": "Complete mastery of reading the soul — the diagnosis of a person's light and darkness, exactly as they stand. He does not accuse and he does not excuse; he *reports*, the way a physician reports a scan, and his report cannot be flattered, bribed, or argued into softness. His power is the precondition of mercy: because his reading is exact, the cleansing that follows it can be exact too — nothing treated that is sound, nothing sound-looking left untreated.",
