  "tale": "Nine thousand snails for a single gram of dye — that was his ancient price, and emperors paid it: he is the color civilizations use when authority must be made visible enough to hold a peace together. The Purple Heart is awarded in his name to this day, binding majesty to sacrifice in one strip of cloth. When that medal is pinned on a nineteen-year-old who carried a friend out of fire, Purple does his deepest work: glory and cost, meeting in one small color.",
