  "origin": "Child of Colors, Violet is the last visible light — the shortest wavelength the human eye can hold, the final band of the rainbow before the spectrum runs off into the unseen. He stands at the far end of his mother's house from Red: where his eldest brother is the first color every tongue learns, Violet is the last one the eye itself can catch. He was appointed to the border, and he has kept it since the first rainbow was read.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Violet fully masters God of Violet in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of violet, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Sensory & Aesthetic Domains\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "Earth's instruments work his border daily. Just past his line, in the unseen country, ultraviolet lamps purify water and make operating rooms safe — medicine done by light nobody can watch working. Astronomers read his shift in distant starlight to measure the universe fleeing outward. And at dusk he is the color of the brief minute when day has ended and night has not taken over — the minute that tells everyone still working outdoors to finish and come home.",
