  "children": [],
  "house": "Darkness's line",
  "origin": "Child of Colors, Brown is the earthly color — soil, wood, and worked land; the color of the ground everything stands on. In his house's great debate he spoke last among the claimants and made the quietest claim: *I am the one the others are standing on while they make theirs.* Nobody paints him on a flag. Nobody names their child for him. He holds the foundation's place in a house of lights, and he holds it without complaint, because that is what foundations are for.",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Brown fully masters God of Brown in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of brown, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Sensory & Aesthetic Domains\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "A handful of his topsoil holds more living organisms than there are people on the planet, and each inch took a century to make. Every harvest in history began in him; every forest stands in him. When rains fail in one country and the harvest holds in another, the difference is often simply him: deep soil against thin. The farmer who builds soil yearly, adding more than he takes, does Earth's most heroic unglamorous work in Brown's color. The world thanks the fruit and forgets the dirt. The dirt does not mind — and the world eats because of it.",
  "job": "To reveal and distinguish brown where needed; to compose its proper operation; and to support the world's wellbeing through responsible mastery of this domain.",
