  "children": [],
  "house": "Darkness's line",
  "origin": "Child of Colors, Orange is the warming color — born between Red's alarm and Yellow's light, and named, unusually, after a fruit, as if Earth insisted on a share in his christening. He is the shade of autumn, harvest, and the lamp at dusk: the hour when the world's work is done and its people are coming home. In his house he kept his claim the shortest: *Red is the alarm; I am the alarm after it has been taught manners — urgency you can sit beside.*",
  "power": "Complete domain authority: God of Orange fully masters God of Orange in its full concept-specific scope: its forms, states, properties, patterns, causes, effects, and natural interactions. This God has complete mastery of god of orange, not automatic sovereignty over the entire category \"Sensory & Aesthetic Domains\" or over another God's distinct concept. Their authority is exercised in service of the world, ysgnutcoh, and their own divine purpose.",
  "tale": "His heroism is the safe arrival. The cone on the wet road that moves a thousand cars kindly past the crew mending the line at midnight; the life vest under the ferry seat; the hunter's vest that keeps him visible to every other gun in the woods. And he is the lamp lit in the window so the returning soul can find the door. Most people, most days, do not need rescue — they need to be warned gently and welcomed home. That ordinary mercy, repeated billions of times, is his whole Earth ministry.",
  "job": "To reveal and distinguish orange where needed; to compose its proper operation; and to support the world's wellbeing through responsible mastery of this domain.",
